3
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:31,970
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译: hj6093 校对&时间轴: tpring

4
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:38,929
国民教育

5
00:00:41,213 --> 00:00:43,377
组织秘书和党主席想见您
The Chief Whip and Party Chairman to see you.

6
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:45,155
各位请坐 我马上就好
Take a seat. I'll be right with you.

7
00:00:46,173 --> 00:00:49,769
伯纳 坐下 我要你也列席
Bernard, take a seat.I want you here for this meeting.

8
00:00:49,934 --> 00:00:52,790
这不是党派事务吗? 这是党派主席和组织秘书
Isn't this a party matter?

9
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:54,208
也是政府工作
It's also a government matter.

10
00:00:54,208 --> 00:00:57,408
是我们的教育政策      国家的还是党派的?
It's about our education policy.The government's or party's?

11
00:00:57,573 --> 00:01:01,361
都一样      抱歉 首相 这可大不一样
It's the same thing.With respect, they're not the same thing.

12
00:01:01,533 --> 00:01:03,923
所以才要开会讨论      好像是党派...
That's why we want the meeting.It seems...

13
00:01:04,094 --> 00:01:06,368
伯纳 坐下
Bernard... sit!

14
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:12,245
不许动
Stay.

15
00:01:14,094 --> 00:01:15,890
问题在哪里?
What's the problem?

16
00:01:16,052 --> 00:01:18,487
教育      你觉得我能怎么办?
Education.What can I do about it?

17
00:01:18,653 --> 00:01:21,850
您是首相啊      对 我知道
You're the PM.Yes, I know.

18
00:01:22,013 --> 00:01:24,733
我没法直接插手教育事务
I have no direct control over education.

19
00:01:24,894 --> 00:01:30,251
我管不了课程 考试 教务长任命 什么都管不了
I don't control the curriculum or exams. Nothing.

20
00:01:30,414 --> 00:01:34,373
可选民觉得都该您负责 您影响力大嘛
The voters hold you responsible for everything.

21
00:01:34,533 --> 00:01:37,537
我烦透了 我原以为当了首相
I'm fed up with it. When I became PM, I thought

22
00:01:37,537 --> 00:01:40,736
就大权在握 结果得到什么? 影响力
I'd have power. And what have I got? Influence.

23
00:01:40,736 --> 00:01:43,492
我控制不了警察 利率
I've got no power over the police, the rates,

24
00:01:43,653 --> 00:01:48,808
欧共体指令 欧洲法庭 我们的法庭 法官 北约
EEC directives, European courts, our courts, the judges, NATO.

25
00:01:48,972 --> 00:01:50,402
我到底有什么权力?
What have I got the power to do?

26
00:01:50,402 --> 00:01:52,987
让我们输掉下次大选的权力
Lose us the next election.

27
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:55,686
您再不管管教育 它就立竿见影了
Which you will if you don't tackle education.

28
00:01:55,853 --> 00:02:00,450
选民们希望管管学术浮夸 学风懒散
The voters want something done about low academic attainment.

29
00:02:00,614 --> 00:02:03,331
性教育      我不是反对性教育
Sex education!I'm not against sex education.

30
00:02:03,492 --> 00:02:06,493
我不是反对课堂上教育孩子生命的真谛
I'm not against children being taught the facts of life in class,

31
00:02:06,493 --> 00:02:08,804
但不能教他们同性恋的技巧啊
but not homosexual technique!

32
00:02:09,492 --> 00:02:13,692
当然 异性恋的技巧也不行      那他们去哪学呢?
Or heterosexual technique.Where should they learn it?

33
00:02:13,854 --> 00:02:16,320
在自行车棚后面 像我们当年一样
Behind the bike sheds like we did!

34
00:02:17,332 --> 00:02:19,368
你是吗?
Did you?

35
00:02:20,052 --> 00:02:22,044
别去管性技巧了
Never mind sexual technique.

36
00:02:22,212 --> 00:02:25,411
有些学校教印度语比教英文还多
Some of our schools are teaching more Hindi than English.

37
00:02:25,573 --> 00:02:28,941
我知道英语更重要 但我不敢公开说
I know English is more important, but I daren't say so

38
00:02:28,941 --> 00:02:30,141
会被人扣上种族主义帽子的
or I'd be accused of racism.

39
00:02:30,141 --> 00:02:32,863
对 可...      上次接见民族事务委员会
When I met the Ethnic Awareness Council,

40
00:02:32,863 --> 00:02:34,648
一位黑人女代表发言时
I happened to glance at my watch

41
00:02:34,648 --> 00:02:36,201
我凑巧看了看表
when a black woman delegate was speaking

42
00:02:36,201 --> 00:02:39,601
马上被指责一举一动充满种族歧视
and I was accused of racist body language.

43
00:02:39,601 --> 00:02:41,164
还有性别歧视
And sexist.

44
00:02:41,332 --> 00:02:45,531
好吧 你们要我怎么办?      请您狠抓教育
What do you want me to do? Get a grip on education.

45
00:02:45,693 --> 00:02:48,890
让亨利把他的教育部好好整治一番
Get Henry to do something about the Department of Education.

46
00:02:49,052 --> 00:02:51,487
不行 他已经给驯服了      开掉他
They've got him house-trained. Sack him.

47
00:02:51,653 --> 00:02:54,121
我不能再来一次内阁动乱了
I can't have another Cabinet convulsion.

48
00:02:54,293 --> 00:02:57,808
那就请在野党党魁夫人来吧      她来干嘛?
Then invite the opposition leader's wife here. What can she do?

49
00:02:57,973 --> 00:03:00,965
量尺寸准备换地毯和窗帘
Start measuring up for carpets and curtains.

50
00:03:03,973 --> 00:03:06,965
好 没问题 今天下午吗?
Yes, right, fine. This afternoon?

51
00:03:07,134 --> 00:03:11,092
伯纳 首相似乎要见我      是的 汉弗莱爵士
Bernard, I believe the PM wants to see me. Yes, Sir Humphrey.

52
00:03:11,253 --> 00:03:14,450
他有什么问题?      教育
What's his problem? Education.

53
00:03:14,614 --> 00:03:18,207
这个嘛 现在后悔也晚了
Well, it's a bit late to do anything about that now.

54
00:03:18,373 --> 00:03:21,366
不 是教育系统问题      我明白了
No, no, the education system. I see.

55
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:25,971
那个也晚了      他觉得他会输掉下次大选的
late to do about that either. he'll lose the next election.

56
00:03:26,134 --> 00:03:30,412
对国家未必是坏事      他没法忽略事实
Worse things could befall the nation. He can't ignore facts.

57
00:03:30,573 --> 00:03:34,567
如果不能忽略事实 他这政客就不用当了
If he can't ignore facts, he's got no business being a politician.

58
00:03:35,693 --> 00:03:38,890
不管怎样 伯纳 他不必担心
Anyway, Bernard, he's got nothing to worry about.

59
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:42,647
我们的教育系统满足了大多数家长的要求
The education system does all most parents require of it.

60
00:03:42,812 --> 00:03:45,532
就是家长上班时 帮他们看孩子
Keeps children out of mischief while they're at work.

61
00:03:45,693 --> 00:03:48,816
对 可从党主席给首相的报告来看
That paper the Party Chairman had suggests

62
00:03:48,816 --> 00:03:51,552
综合素质教育快破产了吧?
the comprehensive system is breaking down.

63
00:03:51,552 --> 00:03:54,219
伯纳 我万万想不到
Bernard, I never thought to hear such language

64
00:03:54,219 --> 00:03:57,963
一个忠实的公务员会说出这种话
from a loyal member of the Civil Service!

65
00:03:57,963 --> 00:04:01,846
你被敌人俘虏了吗?        您说俄国人?
Have you been got at by the enemy? You mean the Russians?

66
00:04:03,653 --> 00:04:06,948
不 伯纳 我说首相的政治顾问
No, Bernard, I mean the PM's political advisor

67
00:04:06,948 --> 00:04:08,401
那个叫韦莱的女人
that Wainwright female.

68
00:04:08,401 --> 00:04:12,035
可综合素质教育是个实验 当然需要规制
Comprehensive education ought to be validated.

69
00:04:12,035 --> 00:04:14,098
当然 但不能一棍子打死啊
Of course, but not invalidated.

70
00:04:14,098 --> 00:04:16,810
可如果它是为了提升教育质量...
But if it was introduced to improve standards...

71
00:04:16,973 --> 00:04:20,170
你怎么会有这个念头?
Whatever gave you that idea?

72
00:04:21,134 --> 00:04:24,966
您是说它是用来抹平阶级差异的?      正是
You mean it was to get rid of class distinction? Precisely!

73
00:04:25,134 --> 00:04:27,329
所以孩子们...      孩子?
So that all children... Children?

74
00:04:27,492 --> 00:04:30,690
关孩子什么事?      我以为...
Who mentioned children? I just...

75
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:34,242
教育部里从来不提孩子
The Department of Education never mentions children!

76
00:04:34,413 --> 00:04:36,885
不不不 伯纳 它是用来抹平
No, no, no, no, Bernard. It was to get rid of

77
00:04:36,885 --> 00:04:40,936
教师的阶级差异的
class distinction in the teaching profession.

78
00:04:40,936 --> 00:04:43,163
提升教师的生活质量
Improve the living standard of teachers,

79
00:04:43,163 --> 00:04:45,556
而不是孩子的教育质量
not the educational standards of children.

80
00:04:45,556 --> 00:04:48,438
提升教师工会会员的工资
Bring the NUT teachers up

81
00:04:48,438 --> 00:04:51,000
让它和他们的死对头
to the salary level of their rivals in

82
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,444
语法学校的全国校长联合会会员持平
the National Association of Schoolmasters in the grammar schools.

83
00:04:53,613 --> 00:04:56,605
可是...      伯纳 工党执政的时候
But the... When there is a Labour government,

84
00:04:56,773 --> 00:05:00,766
教育部夸综合素质教育能抹平阶级差异
the ESD says comprehensives abolish the class system.

85
00:05:00,934 --> 00:05:05,530
等保守党上台 他们就改口夸它价格便宜量又足
When there's Tory, they say it's the cheapest way.

86
00:05:05,694 --> 00:05:08,889
对工党我们解释说 选择性教育造成阶级分化
To Labour, we explain that selective education is divisive

87
00:05:09,052 --> 00:05:12,490
对保守党就解释说 选择性教育贵得离谱
and to the Tories we explain that it is expensive.

88
00:05:13,773 --> 00:05:16,725
这样 我们就能跟教师工会搞好关系
That way, we have a happy relationship with the NUT

89
00:05:16,725 --> 00:05:21,111
关起门来给自家孩子私立教育了
and we educate our own children privately.

90
00:05:21,773 --> 00:05:25,483
但如果政府想改变...      工会不想改变
But if the government wants change... The teaching unions don't.

91
00:05:25,653 --> 00:05:29,249
我们的工作不是说服工会接受政府政策吗?
Isn't it our job to persuade unions to accept government policy?

92
00:05:29,413 --> 00:05:33,565
不 我们的工作是说服政府接受工会政策
No, it is our job to get the government to accept union policy.

93
00:05:33,733 --> 00:05:39,524
因为政府政策说变就变 而工会政策雷打不动
Since government change policy all the time

94
00:05:39,694 --> 00:05:44,165
天经地义的 应该让政府适应工会才对
the government SHOULD be brought in line with the unions.

95
00:05:46,093 --> 00:05:49,165
喂 首相? 好的 他现在就去见您
Yes, PM? Oh, fine. He can see you now.

96
00:05:50,213 --> 00:05:53,591
汉弗莱爵士 他很担心有些事
Sir Humphrey, he's very worried that he seems

97
00:05:53,591 --> 00:05:55,500
他无能为力 也要他负责
responsible for something he can't change.

98
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:58,565
是啊 那还用说 为无能为力的事负责
Yes, I'm sure. Responsibility without power -

99
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:01,850
这是每朝每代的太监的特权
the prerogative of the eunuch throughout the ages.

100
00:06:02,012 --> 00:06:05,562
早安 首相      早安 汉弗莱 你说什么?
PM. Good morning. What were you saying?

101
00:06:05,733 --> 00:06:09,646
没什么 首相 听说您在担心地方教育当局
you're worried about the local education authority.

102
00:06:09,812 --> 00:06:12,756
不 汉弗莱 我是担心国家教育部
No, the Department of Education and Science.

103
00:06:12,756 --> 00:06:15,760
是吗? 我觉得教育部干得很好啊
Indeed? I think the DES does a splendid job.

104
00:06:16,093 --> 00:06:18,974
随你怎么说 睁眼看看现状吧
Look what's happened to education.

105
00:06:18,974 --> 00:06:21,503
这是一篇宗教论文的论题
This is a question from a Religious Studies paper.

106
00:06:21,503 --> 00:06:24,370
“你更喜欢哪个——原子弹或慈善事业?”
"Which do you prefer atom bombs or charity?"

107
00:06:26,293 --> 00:06:28,283
连数学题也政治化了
Even maths is politicised.

108
00:06:28,452 --> 00:06:32,605
“如果英国核武防御每年要花5亿英镑”
"If it costs ? billion a yearfor nuclear defences

109
00:06:32,773 --> 00:06:36,369
“喂饱一名非洲饥童每年要75英镑”
"and ?5 a year to feed a starving African child,

110
00:06:36,533 --> 00:06:39,331
“如果国防部放弃核武器”
"how many children could be saved from starvation

111
00:06:39,494 --> 00:06:43,043
“能救多少非洲孩子的命?”
"if the Ministry of Defence abandoned nuclear weapons?"

112
00:06:44,574 --> 00:06:48,771
很简单 零个 他们会拿钱去买常规武器
That's easy. None. They'd spend it all on conventional weapons.

113
00:06:48,932 --> 00:06:52,768
不管怎样 这只是个算术 5亿除以75就行了
In any case, it's just a sum. Five billion divided by 75.

114
00:06:52,932 --> 00:06:55,447
可孩子们也没学会算算数
But children aren't learning to do the sums.

115
00:06:55,613 --> 00:06:58,713
没错 可地方教育当局也许会说
The local education authorities might argue

116
00:06:58,713 --> 00:07:02,055
他们不必 他们有计算器啊
that they don't need to. They have calculators.

117
00:07:02,055 --> 00:07:04,594
他们总得明白原理吧
They all need to know HOW it's done.

118
00:07:04,594 --> 00:07:07,561
我们都学过基本算术 不是吗?
We were all taught basis arithmetic, weren't we?

119
00:07:07,561 --> 00:07:11,286
是吗? 3947除73等于多少?
Were we? What's 3,947 divided by 73?

120
00:07:11,452 --> 00:07:16,244
呃 我需要纸笔打草稿...得了别管了
Er... Oh, I'd need a pencil and paper to do that.

121
00:07:20,293 --> 00:07:23,682
我刚毕业的时候会的      可现在您用计算器了
I could do it when I left school. Now you'd use a calculator.

122
00:07:23,853 --> 00:07:27,732
这不是重点 看看拉丁文 现在没人懂了吧?
That's not the point. Look at Latin. Hardly anybody knows that now.

123
00:07:28,452 --> 00:07:31,444
Tempora mutantur, nos et mutamur in illis.
"Tempora mutantur, nos et mutamur in illis."

124
00:07:32,932 --> 00:07:34,524
什么?
What?

125
00:07:35,533 --> 00:07:38,764
“时间变化 我们随之而变”      一点不错
Times change and we change with the times. Precisely.

126
00:07:38,932 --> 00:07:42,550
Si tacuisses, philosophus manisses
Si tacuisses, philosophus manisses.

127
00:07:42,550 --> 00:07:44,246
什么意思?
What does that mean?

128
00:07:44,853 --> 00:07:48,846
“请你闭嘴 会显得聪明点”
kept your mouth shut, we might thought you were clever.

129
00:07:49,932 --> 00:07:54,290
你说什么?      不是说您 首相 那是翻译
I beg your pardon? Not you, PM. That's the translation.

130
00:07:54,452 --> 00:07:58,163
没人会以为 汉弗莱爵士会那么说您
No one would have thought Sir Humphrey was saying that about you.

131
00:07:58,333 --> 00:08:00,369
走开 伯纳 求你了
Go away, Bernard, please.

132
00:08:01,574 --> 00:08:02,790
真不敢相信 汉弗莱
I can't believe it.

133
00:08:02,790 --> 00:08:05,333
你是受严格学院式教育长大的
You had a strict academic upbringing.

134
00:08:05,333 --> 00:08:06,950
你居然否认它的价值?
Are you denying the value of it?

135
00:08:06,950 --> 00:08:12,449
有什么用呢? 我跟英国首相说话都用不上
I can't even call upon it in conversation with the PM

136
00:08:12,613 --> 00:08:15,002
这个国家的教育是场灾难
Education in this country is a disaster.

137
00:08:15,173 --> 00:08:19,531
我们应该教会孩子谋生 结果却整天让他们无聊
We're supposed to prepare children for work. 

138
00:08:19,694 --> 00:08:24,528
我倒觉得 无聊是他们谋生的必备技能
being bored stiff was an excellent preparation for work.

139
00:08:26,014 --> 00:08:29,801
毕业时间提高到16岁了 学的却更少了
The school leaving age was raised to 16, but they're learning less.

140
00:08:29,973 --> 00:08:32,441
我们提高毕业年龄 又不是为了多学
We didn't raise it so they'd learn more

141
00:08:32,613 --> 00:08:35,141
而是为了把青少年拦在就业市场外
but to keep teenagers off the job market

142
00:08:35,141 --> 00:08:37,588
以降低失业率
and hold down unemployment figures.

143
00:08:37,588 --> 00:08:39,966
你难道是说 教育一点问题都没有?
Are you saying there's nothing wrong with education?

144
00:08:40,133 --> 00:08:42,114
当然不是 首相 它是个笑话
Of course not. It's a joke.

145
00:08:42,114 --> 00:08:43,693
一直都是个笑话
It's always been a joke.

146
00:08:43,693 --> 00:08:47,765
在地方政务理事会手里 会永远是个笑话
By leaving it in the hands of local councillors

147
00:08:47,932 --> 00:08:49,923
一半理事是您的敌人
Half of them are your enemies

148
00:08:50,093 --> 00:08:54,370
另一半是朋友 却让您觉得还是敌人好
and the other half make you prefer your enemies.

149
00:08:54,533 --> 00:08:58,366
你想说什么?        我是说 教育永远也好转不了
What are you saying? That education will never get any better

150
00:08:58,533 --> 00:09:02,002
只要它还在市政厅那帮笨蛋手里
as long as it's subject to all that tomfoolery in the town halls.

151
00:09:02,173 --> 00:09:05,562
想想要是把国防交给他们 后果如何
Imagine what would happen if you put defence in their hands.

152
00:09:05,732 --> 00:09:08,292
国防?      对 给每个理事会一亿英镑
Defence? Give councils ?00 million each

153
00:09:08,452 --> 00:09:11,416
叫他们自己搞国防 别担心俄国了
and ask them to defend themselves,

154
00:09:11,416 --> 00:09:13,905
不出三周内战就爆发了
we'd have a civil war in three weeks!

155
00:09:14,332 --> 00:09:17,803
别胡思乱想      是吗? 教育就是活例子
You're being silly. Am I? That's what's happened to education.

156
00:09:17,973 --> 00:09:21,400
为什么? 因为没人会以对待国防
And why? Because nobody thinks education

157
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:23,330
的认真劲儿来对待教育
is serious the way defence is serious.

158
00:09:23,330 --> 00:09:24,770
这就是为什么民防系统
So that's why civil defence

159
00:09:24,770 --> 00:09:26,433
交给地方政府吧?
is in local authority hands?

160
00:09:26,433 --> 00:09:28,930
当然 因为大家都知道民防是个笑话
Of course. Because everybody knows it's a joke.

161
00:09:29,093 --> 00:09:34,086
反正不能把重要的事交给那些小丑管
don't leave important matters to those clowns!

162
00:09:34,252 --> 00:09:36,847
鉴于您已经把教育丢给他们管
And as you've left education to them,

163
00:09:37,013 --> 00:09:41,131
只能推断 到目前为止 您没有重视它
you have attached little importance to it.

164
00:09:41,292 --> 00:09:44,569
它当然重要 它能让我输掉下次大选啊
It is important. It could lose me the next election.

165
00:09:46,693 --> 00:09:51,926
我还天真地以为 您是担心我们孩子们的未来呢
I thought you were concerned about the future of children.

166
00:09:52,653 --> 00:09:56,247
我也担心呀 毕竟 他们满18岁就能投票了
Yes, that too. After all, they get the vote at 18.

167
00:09:56,412 --> 00:10:02,203
好 首相 那就中央集权吧 把它从地方收上来
Then, PM, then centralise. Take it away from the local councils.

168
00:10:02,372 --> 00:10:07,371
置于教育部掌管下 您就能有所作为了
Put it under the DES, you could do something about it.

169
00:10:07,371 --> 00:10:11,086
你觉得我行吗? 披荆斩棘 牵着牛角走?
Do you think I could? Grasp the nettle, take the bull by the horns?

170
00:10:11,252 --> 00:10:15,450
首相 如果您披荆斩棘 就没法牵牛角了
You can't take the bull by the horns if you're grasping the nettle.

171
00:10:15,613 --> 00:10:17,365
是吗 伯纳?
Oh, really, Bernard?

172
00:10:18,133 --> 00:10:23,446
我是说 您可以一手斩荆棘 一手牵牛角
grasping the nettle, you could take the bull by one horn

173
00:10:23,613 --> 00:10:26,604
但无法牵两个角 因为您的手不够大
but not both horns because your hand isn't big enough.

174
00:10:26,772 --> 00:10:31,562
如果只牵一个角 又太危险 因为...
 it would be rather dangerous because...

175
00:10:34,093 --> 00:10:40,401
这只是个隐喻矛盾 既然谈的是教育 我...
Well, since we were discussing education, I...

176
00:10:40,401 --> 00:10:41,847
感谢上帝
Thank God!

177
00:10:42,852 --> 00:10:46,129
喂? 您的政治顾问来了
Yes? Your political advisor's outside.

178
00:10:46,292 --> 00:10:49,490
请她进来 伯纳 谢谢 汉弗莱      谢谢您
Send her in, Bernard. Humphrey, thank you. Thank you.

179
00:10:49,653 --> 00:10:51,700
你给了我很多值得咀嚼的问题
You've given me much food for thought.

180
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:55,204
那么 首相 祝您胃口好
In that case, PM, bon app閠it.

181
00:10:56,493 --> 00:10:58,211
亲爱的女士
Dear lady.

182
00:10:58,892 --> 00:11:00,011
什么事 多萝西?
Yes, Dorothy?

183
00:11:00,011 --> 00:11:03,132
关于您西北地区访问的日程
My notes for your tour of the north-west.

184
00:11:03,132 --> 00:11:05,412
您视察医院和工厂的安排 首相
Visits to hospitals and factories.

185
00:11:05,573 --> 00:11:08,348
对 在边缘选区(拉锯战选区)拉选票
Drumming up votes in marginal constituencies.

186
00:11:08,348 --> 00:11:09,470
不行 首相
No!

187
00:11:09,470 --> 00:11:10,285
怎么不行?
Why not?

188
00:11:10,285 --> 00:11:13,101
如果是政府的访问 我就能跟您去
I'm coming with you if it's a government tour.

189
00:11:13,101 --> 00:11:15,247
如果是拉选票 就是党务
If it's canvassing marginals,

190
00:11:15,247 --> 00:11:17,320
我就不能去了 财政部也不报销
I can't come and the Treasury can't pay.

191
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,514
这是政府访问 伯纳
It's a government visit. It's coincidence

192
00:11:18,514 --> 00:11:20,995
只是恰好都定点在边缘选区
that all the stop-offs are in marginals.

193
00:11:21,343 --> 00:11:25,530
那就没问题了      那好
Well, that's all right, then. That's OK.

194
00:11:25,693 --> 00:11:28,412
多萝西 对教育我能做什么? 快一点
What can I do about education? Quickly.

195
00:11:28,573 --> 00:11:30,480
您是要真干 还是显得您在干?
You mean do or appear to do?

196
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:33,104
显得在干 我当然没法真干
Appear to do. I can't do, obviously.

197
00:11:35,127 --> 00:11:38,564
短期来说 我们可以让您上电视 展示教育成就
we could get you on TV associated with something successful.

198
00:11:38,732 --> 00:11:42,089
好 有机会吗?      我想到一个
Is there something? I had thought of this for your schedule.

199
00:11:42,252 --> 00:11:47,042
您塞进日程吧      圣玛丽学校青年企业计划
You could fit it in. St Margaret's School Young Enterprise Scheme.

200
00:11:47,212 --> 00:11:50,126
对 学校自设制造分销厂
It's set up its own manufacturing company.

201
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:52,855
制造干酪板 镇纸 吐司架等等
They make cheeseboards, paperweights, toast racks,

202
00:11:52,855 --> 00:11:56,560
自己销售 然后在商业课上追踪整个流程
sell them and track the operation in their business-study classes.

203
00:11:56,732 --> 00:11:59,303
与当地商人合作 还有家长
They involve local businessmen. Parents help.

204
00:11:59,303 --> 00:12:01,438
貌似不错 花销大吗?
Does it cost a lot?

205
00:12:01,438 --> 00:12:05,530
不 还赚钱呢      这不是教孩子唯利是图吗?
Isn't it teaching them to be rather grasping?

206
00:12:05,693 --> 00:12:08,089
不 赚的钱捐给了当地慈善机构
No, they give the money to local charity.

207
00:12:08,089 --> 00:12:09,930
好极了 我要去
Fine, I'll do it.

208
00:12:10,053 --> 00:12:15,649
给电视台安排充足时间拍我...拍摄整个访问
Make sure the TV crews have plenty of time to cover me... 

209
00:12:15,812 --> 00:12:20,602
给我写个简短的讲话 20秒 新闻短讯式的
Write me a speech with a snappy, 20-second piece 

210
00:12:20,772 --> 00:12:23,571
这能拉到点席位      首相?
That should win back a few seats. PM.

211
00:12:23,732 --> 00:12:28,443
给国民教育的负责人们做点榜样 伯纳
give a lead to those responsible for the nation's education

212
00:12:28,613 --> 00:12:30,807
当然 首相
Of course, PM.

213
00:12:30,973 --> 00:12:34,363
最后 今晨 首相在西北之行的末尾
<i>(NEWSREADER) Finally, the PM visited St Margaret's School</i>

214
00:12:34,533 --> 00:12:36,524
视察了圣玛丽学校
<i>on his north-western tour.</i>

215
00:12:36,693 --> 00:12:39,685
该校自办了一座制造工厂
<i>The school has set up a manufacturing business</i>

216
00:12:39,852 --> 00:12:44,290
孩子们生产各种木工产品 出售给当地社区
<i>where the children make a variety of goods</i>

217
00:12:44,452 --> 00:12:49,573
孩子们自己销售 开拓市场 并以学来的经验
<i>The children do their own sales and marketing</i>

218
00:12:49,732 --> 00:12:53,772
为数学和商业课程打下基础
<i>as a basis for their maths and business studies.</i>

219
00:12:53,932 --> 00:12:57,972
他们赠送给首相一件产品的样品
<i>The PM was presented with an example of the school's output.</i>

220
00:12:59,212 --> 00:13:01,680
总而言之 我要祝贺你们
In conclusion, I must congratulate you

221
00:13:01,852 --> 00:13:06,290
努力的工作 良好的纪律和成功的企业
<i>on the discipline and the success of your enterprise.</i>

222
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:09,286
你们是英国教育界的楷模
<i>You've set an example in British education </i>

223
00:13:09,286 --> 00:13:12,198
其它学校都该向你们学习
which other schools would do well to follow.

224
00:13:12,198 --> 00:13:15,240
我们需要更多圣玛丽学校
<i>We need more schools like St Margaret's </i>

225
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:18,048
我会永远珍惜你们的礼物
and I shall always treasure your present.

226
00:13:18,173 --> 00:13:21,961
没有首相会轻易抛弃他的席位
<i>No PM ever lost a seat if he could help itl</i>

227
00:13:24,693 --> 00:13:28,082
这里是BBC六点新闻
<i>(NEWSREADER) And that was the six o'clock news from the BBC.</i>

228
00:13:31,053 --> 00:13:33,520
我觉得还不错 你觉得呢?        很好
I thought that was OK, didn't you? Fine.

229
00:13:33,693 --> 00:13:36,490
我的俏皮话反响不错      是我的俏皮话
My joke went down well. MY joke!

230
00:13:37,493 --> 00:13:39,402
反正比4频道报得好
Better than Channel 4 coverage.

231
00:13:39,402 --> 00:13:42,654
他们没叫它“首相的西北之行”
They didn't describe it as the PM's tour of the north-west.

232
00:13:42,654 --> 00:13:46,600
而叫它“吉姆哈克的边缘选区之行”
They said, "Jim Hacker touring the marginal constituencies."

233
00:13:46,772 --> 00:13:48,158
这是事实 不是吗?
That's true, isn't it?

234
00:13:48,158 --> 00:13:51,359
对 但他们不该明说 这是偏见报道
But they shouldn't say it. It's biased reporting!

235
00:13:51,359 --> 00:13:54,602
报道事实?      访问边缘选区不算错啊
Reporting the facts? Nothing wrong with visiting the marginals.

236
00:13:54,772 --> 00:13:58,526
那他们说的还是事实      明说出来就是有偏见
What they said was still true. It was still biased to say it!

237
00:13:58,693 --> 00:14:00,765
亲爱的 我对你的偏执狂不感兴趣
I'm not interested in your paranoia.

238
00:14:00,765 --> 00:14:03,063
我对那所学校感兴趣
I was interested in that school.

239
00:14:03,063 --> 00:14:05,183
对 父母们排着队想把孩子送进去
Parents queue up to get their children into it.

240
00:14:05,183 --> 00:14:08,159
真遗憾不能全收 来点咖啡?
Pity they can't all get in. Coffee?

241
00:14:08,159 --> 00:14:11,731
太好了      为什么不能多送些孩子进去?
Lovely. Why can't more parents send children there?

242
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:14,691
没地方了      有啊 学校的数量在下降
No room. There is. School numbers are falling.

243
00:14:14,852 --> 00:14:17,765
那就排挤其它学校了      那又怎样?
That'd mean poaching the other schools. So what?

244
00:14:17,932 --> 00:14:20,241
其它学校没生源 会关门的
The other schools would have to close.

245
00:14:20,412 --> 00:14:23,290
太好了 圣玛丽就能把它们的房子也接管了
Great! St Margaret's could take over their buildings.

246
00:14:23,452 --> 00:14:26,285
亲爱的 这不公平      对谁?
Darling, that wouldn't be fair. Who to?

247
00:14:26,452 --> 00:14:28,955
对那些要关闭的学校里的老师
The teachers in the schools that had to close.

248
00:14:28,955 --> 00:14:32,790
好老师可以去热门学校啊
Good ones could teach at the popular schools.

249
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:36,207
那差劲老师呢? 对他们不公平
What about the bad teachers? It wouldn't be fair on them.

250
00:14:36,372 --> 00:14:40,412
哪个更重要? 孩子们 还是差劲老师的工作?
are the bad teachers' jobs more important?

251
00:14:40,573 --> 00:14:42,408
亲爱的 这…不太好
Darling, it's... it's no good. Who's to say

252
00:14:42,408 --> 00:14:45,689
谁来评定老师好坏呢? 这行不通
who are the bad teachers? It just wouldn't work.

253
00:14:45,689 --> 00:14:48,923
怎么行不通?      就是行不通
Why not? Well... it wouldn't work.

254
00:14:49,093 --> 00:14:51,129
怎么行不通?      怎么讲?
Why not? What do you mean?

255
00:14:51,292 --> 00:14:55,239
把学校比做大夫 国民保健体系
Suppose schools were like doctors. In the NHS,

256
00:14:55,239 --> 00:14:57,847
允许病人选择大夫 是不是?
you choose which doctor to go to, don't you?

257
00:14:57,847 --> 00:14:59,881
是啊       他按病人人数领薪水
Yes. And he gets paid per patient.

258
00:15:00,332 --> 00:15:02,871
为什么不能对学校也这样呢?
Why don't we do the same with schools?

259
00:15:02,871 --> 00:15:05,575
弄个国民教育体系
Have a National Education Service.

260
00:15:05,575 --> 00:15:09,091
家长选择学校 学校按学生数目来收钱
Parents could choose the schools

261
00:15:09,252 --> 00:15:11,892
太对了      会爆发抗议的
Exactly! There'd be an outcry.

262
00:15:12,053 --> 00:15:15,761
家长吗?      不是家长 是教育部
From the parents? No, from the Department of Education.

263
00:15:15,932 --> 00:15:17,759
好吧 哪方手里选票多?
I see. And who has the most votes?

264
00:15:17,759 --> 00:15:19,707
不行 教育部会封杀它的
The DES would block it.

265
00:15:19,707 --> 00:15:22,086
好啊 除掉他们好了      什么?
Fine, get rid of them. What?

266
00:15:22,252 --> 00:15:25,848
除掉教育部好了      我不明白
Get rid of the Department of Education. I don't understand you.

267
00:15:26,013 --> 00:15:30,450
除掉它 取消它 扔掉它 解除它
Get rid of it, abolish it, remove it, expunge it,

268
00:15:30,613 --> 00:15:34,207
废除它 清除它 根除它
eliminate it, eradicate it, exterminate it!

269
00:15:34,372 --> 00:15:37,763
除掉它      除掉它?
Get rid of it! Get rid of it?

270
00:15:37,932 --> 00:15:40,287
对      我不能这么做
Yes. I couldn't do that.

271
00:15:40,452 --> 00:15:43,843
为什么不能? 它有什么用?      我能做到啊
Why not? What does it do? I could do that.

272
00:15:45,093 --> 00:15:47,481
把事情都交给地方当局
Local government could administer the lot.

273
00:15:47,653 --> 00:15:51,850
设一个学校监察委员会 其它职责交给环境部
We could have a Board of School Inspectors.

274
00:15:52,013 --> 00:15:52,989
然后我就可以把那个
I could send that house-trained

275
00:15:52,989 --> 00:15:55,588
被驯服的白痴大臣扔到上院去
idiot Henry to the House of Lords.

276
00:15:55,973 --> 00:15:58,533
天啊 汉弗莱会怎么说呢
Golly. I wonder what Humphrey will say.

277
00:15:58,693 --> 00:16:01,890
不管他怎么说 我希望亲眼看您告诉他
Whatever he says, I want to be there when you tell him.

278
00:16:02,053 --> 00:16:06,126
来见证政治愿望对抗行政愿望?
the political will and the administrative will?

279
00:16:06,292 --> 00:16:10,763
我想这会是政治愿望对抗行政失望
the political will and the administrative won't.

280
00:16:14,452 --> 00:16:17,763
您找我 首相?        汉弗莱 进来 请坐
You sent for me, PM? Humphrey, come in. Sit down.

281
00:16:17,932 --> 00:16:23,290
我有个新点子问你 我想到怎么改革教育系统了
I've realised how to reform the educational system.

282
00:16:23,973 --> 00:16:27,682
太好了 首相
Excellent, PM.

283
00:16:27,852 --> 00:16:32,290
我准备让家长选择把孩子送到哪所学校去
I'm going to let parents move their children.

284
00:16:33,212 --> 00:16:37,923
您是说 经过申请 审查 聆讯和上诉过程后吗?
after application, scrutiny, tribunal hearing and appeals?

285
00:16:38,093 --> 00:16:42,883
不 想送就送了      对不起 我没听懂
No, just move them whenever they want to.

286
00:16:43,053 --> 00:16:45,520
本届政府将让家长自主决定
This government will let parents decide

287
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:47,815
把孩子送到哪所学校
which schools to send their children to.

288
00:16:48,013 --> 00:16:50,810
首相 您不是认真的吧
PM, you can't be serious!

289
00:16:50,973 --> 00:16:53,361
我是啊       这也太荒谬了
I am. But it's preposterous!

290
00:16:53,533 --> 00:16:57,002
怎么?      不能指望家长来做决定
Why? You can't expect parents to make these choices.

291
00:16:57,173 --> 00:17:01,131
家长哪知道哪所学校最好呢?
How on earth would parents know which schools are best?

292
00:17:01,292 --> 00:17:03,087
你上的哪所学校 汉弗莱?
Which school did you go to, Humphrey?

293
00:17:03,087 --> 00:17:05,705
温切斯特公学(牛津附中)
Winchester.

294
00:17:05,705 --> 00:17:08,486
它好吗?      学校中的极品
Was it good? Oh, excellent, of course.

295
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:12,042
谁帮你选的?      自然是我父母
Who chose it? My parents, naturally.

296
00:17:14,173 --> 00:17:18,884
这可不一样 首相 我父母是有鉴察力的人士
Now, that's different, PM. My parents were discerning people.

297
00:17:19,053 --> 00:17:22,886
普通人怎么知道该把孩子送到哪里
ordinary people don't know where to send children.

298
00:17:23,053 --> 00:17:26,203
为什么?      他们怎么分辨?
Why not? Well, how could they tell?

299
00:17:26,373 --> 00:17:27,848
他们自然知道自己的孩子
They could tell if their kids

300
00:17:27,848 --> 00:17:31,089
会不会读写算 学校口碑如何
could read, write and do sums

301
00:17:31,089 --> 00:17:32,283
还有考试成绩好不好
and if the exam results were good.

302
00:17:32,452 --> 00:17:34,489
考试成绩不是一切 首相      没错
Exam results aren't everything. True.

303
00:17:34,653 --> 00:17:39,443
讨厌学院教育的家长 可以把孩子送到特长学校
Parents can pick progressive schools.

304
00:17:39,614 --> 00:17:43,810
可家长没资格做这些选择
But parents have no qualifications to make these choices.

305
00:17:43,973 --> 00:17:49,365
老师都有专业素养 家长最没资格培养孩子了
Parents are the worst people to bring up children.

306
00:17:50,373 --> 00:17:52,777
他们没有认证 没受过训练
They've no qualifications, no training.

307
00:17:52,777 --> 00:17:55,745
教师没有资格不许教书
You don't expect untrained teachers to teach.

308
00:17:55,745 --> 00:17:57,803
家长也应该不许
The same should apply to parents.

309
00:17:57,973 --> 00:18:02,172
生孩子之前 家长应该培训?      不 那不是问题
Before having children, they should be trained?

310
00:18:02,332 --> 00:18:05,131
生孩子的训练人人都受过
They've all been trained to HAVE kids.

311
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:08,490
性教育课早就成为标准课程了
Sex-education classes have been standard for some years.

312
00:18:08,653 --> 00:18:10,644
是吗 也许我们能改进一下
Perhaps we could do better.

313
00:18:10,812 --> 00:18:13,870
为了生孩子 该让他们通过考试
Before people can have children, we should make them sit exams -

314
00:18:13,870 --> 00:18:15,405
笔试或实践考察
written and practical.

315
00:18:15,405 --> 00:18:20,243
或者两样都考 然后发个养孩子执照
Perhaps both. Then they could be issued with breeding licences.

316
00:18:22,373 --> 00:18:25,763
您真幽默 首相
Oh, very droll, PM.

317
00:18:25,932 --> 00:18:30,768
可我是认真的 家长不合格的是带孩子
It's looking after children that parents are not qualified for.

318
00:18:30,932 --> 00:18:35,085
所以他们不懂得该把孩子送到哪 行不通的
That's why they have no idea which schools to choose

319
00:18:35,252 --> 00:18:38,357
那国民保健呢? 没有医学文凭
What about the Health Service? People choose

320
00:18:38,357 --> 00:18:40,823
人们也能自己选医生
their doctor without medical qualifications.

321
00:18:40,823 --> 00:18:42,489
是啊 那是不一样的      怎么?
Ah, yes, well, that's different. How?

322
00:18:42,653 --> 00:18:47,250
医生么...病人又不是家长 亲爱的女士
Well, doctors are... The patients aren't parents, dear lady.

323
00:18:47,413 --> 00:18:50,723
哦 是吗? 何以见得呢 小汉?
Oh, really? What makes you think that, Humpy?

324
00:18:52,973 --> 00:18:55,964
两码事 话说回来 老实告诉你
Not as such. In any case, as a matter of fact,

325
00:18:56,134 --> 00:19:01,332
我觉得让病人选医生也不对 太混乱了
letting people choose doctors is a very bad idea

326
00:19:01,493 --> 00:19:05,884
把人们交给初诊医生分配更有条理 也更公平
Much tidier to allocate people to GPs, much fairer.

327
00:19:06,053 --> 00:19:10,730
每个人就有同样的机会碰到蹩脚大夫了
Then everyone has an equal chance of getting the bad doctors.

328
00:19:10,893 --> 00:19:15,091
这样啊      总之 我们谈的不是医疗 是教育
I see. In any case, we're talking about education.

329
00:19:15,252 --> 00:19:17,243
恕我直言 首相
With respect, PM,

330
00:19:17,413 --> 00:19:20,922
我认为教育部会对您的新颖建议
I think that the DES will react with some caution

331
00:19:20,922 --> 00:19:22,908
作出谨慎反应的
to your rather novel proposals.

332
00:19:22,908 --> 00:19:26,924
你是说他们会封杀它      他们会慎重考虑
You mean they'll block it. They will give it urgent consideration

333
00:19:27,094 --> 00:19:31,086
并坚决对所有建议作出彻底和严格的审查
insist on a thorough and examination of the proposals

334
00:19:31,252 --> 00:19:34,723
结合详细的可行性研究和预算分析
allied to a detailed feasibility study and budget analysis

335
00:19:34,893 --> 00:19:39,922
拟定一份参考方案 递交各有关部门
producing a consultative document for consideration

336
00:19:40,094 --> 00:19:43,687
请他们作出评论和建议 汇总成一份简报
and seeking comments and recommendations to be included in a brief

337
00:19:43,852 --> 00:19:47,926
送给一系列工作组 分别独立研究
for a series of working parties who will produce individual studies

338
00:19:48,094 --> 00:19:52,086
基于其调查报告 起草一份更加包罗万象的文件
which will provide the background for a more wide-ranging document

339
00:19:52,252 --> 00:19:58,010
据此判定 该建议是否能进入下一步骤
considering whether or not the proposal should be taken forward

340
00:19:58,173 --> 00:20:01,245
你是说他们会封杀它      是啊
You mean they'll block it. Yeah.

341
00:20:02,212 --> 00:20:03,964
没问题      我们早知道你会这么说
No problem. We thought you'd say that.

342
00:20:04,134 --> 00:20:05,806
我们有办法对付      哦 是吗?
We have a solution. Oh, yes?

343
00:20:05,973 --> 00:20:07,725
我们要废除教育部
We'll abolish the DES.

344
00:20:10,332 --> 00:20:12,607
什么?      我们要废除它
I'm sorry? We'll abolish it.

345
00:20:12,772 --> 00:20:14,923
废除?      为什么不?
Abolish it? Why not?

346
00:20:15,094 --> 00:20:17,402
废除教育部?
Abolish Education and Science?!

347
00:20:17,573 --> 00:20:20,161
我们的文明的末日来临了
That'd be the end of civilisation as we know it!

348
00:20:20,161 --> 00:20:23,004
只废除部门 教育还是会兴旺发达的
Only the department. Education will flourish.

349
00:20:23,004 --> 00:20:25,326
没有政府部门管理? 不可能
With no government department? Impossible!

350
00:20:25,326 --> 00:20:28,138
汉弗莱 政府部门好比墓碑
Departments are tombstones.

351
00:20:28,138 --> 00:20:30,810
工业部标志着工业的坟墓
The Department of Industry marks the grave of industry,

352
00:20:30,973 --> 00:20:33,770
就业部是就业的坟墓
the Department of Employment, that of employment,

353
00:20:33,932 --> 00:20:37,129
环境部是环境的坟墓
the Department of Environment, that of the environment.

354
00:20:37,292 --> 00:20:42,163
教育部标志着英国教育的尸体埋葬于此
And the DES marks where the corpse of education is buried.

355
00:20:42,332 --> 00:20:44,801
教育部都干什么? 它扮演什么角色?
What does the DES do? What's its role?

356
00:20:44,973 --> 00:20:47,692
我简直不知从何说起 首相
I hardly know where to begin!

357
00:20:47,852 --> 00:20:50,810
它制订方针政策 它集中拨款
It lays down guidelines, it centralises

358
00:20:50,973 --> 00:20:56,172
分发到教育当局 大学奖学金委员会 它设立标准
and channels money into education authorities  it sets standards!

359
00:20:56,332 --> 00:20:59,300
它设置课程吗?      不 可它很乐意代劳
Does it set the curriculum? It would like to!

360
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:01,572
选择教研组长?      不...
Select and change head teachers?

361
00:21:01,572 --> 00:21:03,203
维修学校建筑?
Maintain school buildings?

362
00:21:03,203 --> 00:21:05,352
不...      主管考试吗?
No... Set exams?

363
00:21:05,352 --> 00:21:07,070
不...      它选择学生吗?
No... Does it choose the children?

364
00:21:07,070 --> 00:21:11,143
不 可是...      那它怎么影响学校里的孩子呢?
How does it affect what a child does at school?

365
00:21:11,143 --> 00:21:13,192
它提供60％资金
It supplies 60% of the cash.

366
00:21:13,192 --> 00:21:16,761
为什么不能由财政部拨款到学校呢?
Why can't the cash go from the Treasury to the schools?

367
00:21:16,932 --> 00:21:19,277
我们真需要2000名公务员
Do we need 2,000 civil servants

368
00:21:19,277 --> 00:21:20,942
把钱从甲发到乙手上吗?
to funnel money from A to B?

369
00:21:20,942 --> 00:21:24,611
教育部也为教育建立法规制度
The DES also creates a legislative framework for education.

370
00:21:24,772 --> 00:21:28,142
没多少立法吧 环境部就可以做
Not much legislation. Environment could do that.

371
00:21:28,142 --> 00:21:30,574
地方当局还有些事也交给他们
They deal with other local authority matters.

372
00:21:30,574 --> 00:21:32,203
首相 您不是认真的吧
You can't be serious!

373
00:21:32,373 --> 00:21:37,082
那谁来评估发展规划 员工变动 生源变更
Who'd assess forward planning and staffing variations

374
00:21:37,252 --> 00:21:40,245
计划城乡的学校密度呢?
density of schooling required in urban and rural areas?

375
00:21:40,413 --> 00:21:42,767
谁来确保一切正常运转呢?
Who'd make sure everything ran properly?

376
00:21:42,767 --> 00:21:44,934
全国2500所私立学校
2,500 private schools

377
00:21:44,934 --> 00:21:48,571
每天都在自己处理这些 根本不靠教育部
seem to solve these without any help from the DES.

378
00:21:48,732 --> 00:21:51,327
他们能灵活地随机应变
They respond to changing circumstances.

379
00:21:51,493 --> 00:21:54,884
供求关系而已 很简单       那谁计划将来呢?
Supply and demand. It's easy. Who would plan for the future?

380
00:21:55,053 --> 00:21:58,044
这教育现状是教育部计划出来的?
Education today is what the department planned?

381
00:21:58,212 --> 00:22:00,966
当...不 当然不是
Well, of... No, of course not!

382
00:22:01,134 --> 00:22:05,126
教育部还干别的吗?      这...这...
Is there anything else that the DES does? Well, it... it...

383
00:22:06,173 --> 00:22:09,768
好 那我们不需要它了 是吗? 完毕
Well, we don't need it, then, do we? QED.

384
00:22:11,094 --> 00:22:13,288
(拉丁文)证明完毕
Quod erat demonstrandum.

385
00:22:16,452 --> 00:22:18,922
我实在...简直不堪设想
I really... Quite unthinkable.

386
00:22:19,094 --> 00:22:24,611
废除部门的先例一开 文明的基石就垮塌了
Once they start abolishing departments, the civilisation crumble.

387
00:22:24,772 --> 00:22:29,482
野蛮人就会入侵       倒退到黑暗时代
Barbarians at the gates. The return of the Dark Ages.

388
00:22:29,653 --> 00:22:33,442
你当内阁秘书时 爆发过这种危机吗?
Did anything like this crop up when you were Cabinet Secretary?

389
00:22:33,614 --> 00:22:38,846
没有 我们允许他们合并部门 但那没问题
No. We let them amalgamate departments, but that worked very well.

390
00:22:39,013 --> 00:22:41,606
当然了 保留所有的职员
Yes, quite. You keep the existing staff

391
00:22:41,772 --> 00:22:45,971
最高处再加一层统筹领导机构
an extra layer of coordinating management at the top.

392
00:22:46,134 --> 00:22:52,241
正是 但你必须阻止对教育部的清算 汉弗莱
Exactly. But you have to stop the liquidation of the DES

393
00:22:52,413 --> 00:22:55,609
试过抹黑提议者的名声吗?
Have you tried discrediting the person who proposed it?

394
00:22:55,772 --> 00:22:58,114
没用 是那个叫韦莱的女人
No point. It was the Wainwright female,

395
00:22:58,114 --> 00:23:00,678
所以首相当成他自己的主意了
so he's passing it off as his own idea.

396
00:23:00,678 --> 00:23:02,977
扭曲背景事实呢?
Discrediting the facts behind it?

397
00:23:02,977 --> 00:23:06,315
这是个政治主张 所以跟事实无关
It's a political idea, so facts don't come into it.

398
00:23:08,094 --> 00:23:11,687
调整数据?      建议里没数据
Massaging the figures? No figures are involved.

399
00:23:11,852 --> 00:23:15,687
但很难让首相明白 这是个坏主意
But it's hard to get the PM to see that it's a bad idea.

400
00:23:15,852 --> 00:23:20,448
当然 这其实是个好主意 只是不能照办
Of course. It's actually a very good idea. It just mustn't happen.

401
00:23:21,452 --> 00:23:24,639
我不懂我们为什么不能照办
I wonder if we oughtn't to play along with it -

402
00:23:24,639 --> 00:23:27,286
为了全国孩子的利益
in the interests of the nation's children.

403
00:23:27,286 --> 00:23:28,886
管他全国孩子呢
Never mind the nation's children.

404
00:23:28,886 --> 00:23:31,274
我们教育部的同僚怎么办?
What about our colleagues at the DES?

405
00:23:31,274 --> 00:23:34,131
当然 对不起       汉弗莱 我们挑明了说
Of course. Sorry. Let's be clear about this.

406
00:23:34,292 --> 00:23:38,002
唯一会喜欢这主意的就是家长和孩子们
The only people who'll like this idea are the parents

407
00:23:38,173 --> 00:23:41,370
其它有关部门都会反对它
Everyone who counts will be against it.

408
00:23:41,533 --> 00:23:43,888
教师工会      地方当局
Teachers' unions. Local authorities.

409
00:23:44,053 --> 00:23:48,091
教育口的媒体       当然 还有教育部自己
Educational press. And, of course, the DES.

410
00:23:48,252 --> 00:23:53,885
那我们用什么策略?      可以靠工会扰乱学校
Unions can be counted on to disrupt the schools.

411
00:23:54,053 --> 00:23:57,568
然后上电视宣称 是政府导致了混乱
And go on TV saying the government are causing the disruption.

412
00:23:57,732 --> 00:24:01,843
好极了 地方当局会威胁
Good. Local councils will threaten to

413
00:24:01,843 --> 00:24:04,312
发动地方党派反对政府
turn the constituency parties against the government.

414
00:24:04,312 --> 00:24:07,966
好 教育部会拖延每个步骤
The Department of Education will delay every stage of the process

415
00:24:08,134 --> 00:24:11,330
把能让政府难堪的消息都漏出去
and leak anything that embarrasses the government.

416
00:24:11,493 --> 00:24:14,884
我们信息自由运动会助一臂之力的
We can help with that at the Campaign for Freedom of Information.

417
00:24:15,053 --> 00:24:16,806
谢谢 阿诺德
Thank you, Arnold.

418
00:24:17,852 --> 00:24:19,649
啊 谢谢
Ah, thanks.

419
00:24:21,693 --> 00:24:26,243
但我们真正的...谢谢 比利 我们的论点是什么?
But what are we actually... Thank you, Billy. What's our argument?

420
00:24:26,893 --> 00:24:31,922
显然 这项新提议会摧毁我们的教育体系
this new proposal will destroy our educational system.

421
00:24:32,094 --> 00:24:36,290
人人都知道它已经毁了      哦 我们会说...
Everybody knows it's destroyed already. Well, we will say...

422
00:24:36,452 --> 00:24:38,298
对不起 媒体会说
Sorry, the press will say

423
00:24:38,298 --> 00:24:42,129
是政府对教育部的干预摧毁了它
that it's government interference in the DES that destroyed it

424
00:24:42,129 --> 00:24:44,886
而且这个新计划只会雪上加霜
and that this new plan will make things worse.

425
00:24:45,053 --> 00:24:48,886
这样能行吗?      一向有效
Will that do the trick? It always has in the past.

426
00:24:49,053 --> 00:24:52,298
对 但这次是政治压力比较强
But this time the political pressure is stronger.

427
00:24:52,298 --> 00:24:56,121
那你得找件政治武器来对抗
You must find a political weapon to fight it with.

428
00:24:56,973 --> 00:25:00,328
你建议什么政治武器呢 阿诺德?
What political weapon did you have in mind, Arnold?

429
00:25:00,893 --> 00:25:04,089
我? 这是你该操心的了 汉弗莱
I? That is your concern, Humphrey.

430
00:25:04,452 --> 00:25:07,135
是你证明自己
Your chance to prove yourself worthy

431
00:25:07,135 --> 00:25:10,717
担得起如此高位的机会
of the high office to which you've been called.

432
00:25:16,332 --> 00:25:18,972
汉弗莱爵士 首相在等您      什么事?
The PM's ready to see you. What's it about?

433
00:25:19,134 --> 00:25:23,524
恐怕是废除教育部的事      真该死
The abolition of the DES, I'm afraid. This is going to be bloody.

434
00:25:23,693 --> 00:25:27,288
对 有件小事我想先请教您      重要吗 伯纳?
There's a minor matter I need your advice... Is it important?

435
00:25:27,452 --> 00:25:29,841
不重要 但很紧急      快说 什么事?
Not important but urgent. What is it?

436
00:25:30,013 --> 00:25:33,109
您知道首相视察的那所企业学校吗
You know that enterprise school the PM visited,

437
00:25:33,109 --> 00:25:34,849
送他凳子的那所      知道
when they gave him that stool?

438
00:25:34,849 --> 00:25:38,812
刚查出他们工厂的木料...是偷来的
It's just come to light that the wood they were using was stolen.

439
00:25:38,973 --> 00:25:40,964
伯纳 这很难...
Bernard, this is hardly...

440
00:25:43,893 --> 00:25:45,690
偷来的?
Stolen?

441
00:25:45,852 --> 00:25:50,687
对 是政府财产 去年一个青年培训车间里失窃的
Yes, it was government property stolen

442
00:25:51,653 --> 00:25:53,644
万万想不到啊
How shocking.

443
00:25:54,893 --> 00:25:58,489
已经通报教育部了 因为偷窃发生在学校里
It was referred to the DES, as the theft came to light at a school.

444
00:25:58,653 --> 00:26:01,803
他们不知道是否该起诉 很抱歉打扰...
They don't know whether to prosecute. Sorry to bother...

445
00:26:01,973 --> 00:26:04,361
没关系 伯纳
Don't mention it, Bernard.

446
00:26:07,094 --> 00:26:09,085
领我进去
Show me in.

447
00:26:11,252 --> 00:26:14,451
进来 汉弗莱 进来进来 请坐
Come in, Humphrey. Come in, come in! Sit down.

448
00:26:14,614 --> 00:26:18,491
今天只有一项日程——废除教育部
Only one item on the agenda today the abolition of the DES.

449
00:26:18,653 --> 00:26:23,602
实际上 如果只有一件事 那叫议程
Actually, if there's only one item, it's an agenDUM.

450
00:26:23,772 --> 00:26:28,243
我想首相还达不到拉丁文第二变位的程度
I don't think the PM's got as far as the second declension.

451
00:26:28,413 --> 00:26:31,839
我不在乎你强词夺理一回
I don't mind your scoring cheap debating points

452
00:26:31,839 --> 00:26:34,548
反正教育部一役你已经输了
since you've already lost the battle of the DES.

453
00:26:34,548 --> 00:26:36,884
教育部会大发雷霆的 首相
The DES will be very upset.

454
00:26:36,884 --> 00:26:38,804
管它呢 他们就快灭亡了
Does it matter since they'll cease to exist?

455
00:26:38,804 --> 00:26:41,844
解散过程会持续几年 他们会以死相拼的
The process will take a few years. They'll fight tooth and nail.

456
00:26:42,013 --> 00:26:45,210
他们能把我怎样?      他们是个令人生畏的部门
What can they do to me? They're a formidable department.

457
00:26:45,373 --> 00:26:48,682
我是个令人生畏的首相      您确实是 首相
I am a formidable PM. Indeed you are.

458
00:26:48,852 --> 00:26:51,652
但您也许还需要他们的合作
But you might still need their cooperation.

459
00:26:51,812 --> 00:26:56,522
合作? 教育部的? 别开玩笑了
Cooperation? From the Department of Education? Don't make me laugh!

460
00:26:57,373 --> 00:27:01,365
好吧 好吧 那我就由他们去起诉了
Fine, fine. I'll tell them to go ahead with the prosecution, then.

461
00:27:02,614 --> 00:27:06,652
什么起诉?        哦 这点小事不值得打扰您
What prosecution? Oh, it's hardly worth bothering you with.

462
00:27:06,812 --> 00:27:10,044
就是上周电视上 您视察的企业学校
That enterprise school where you were televised last week.

463
00:27:10,212 --> 00:27:14,205
怎么?      那些利润...其它学校的楷模...
Yes? The profits... A model for other schools...

464
00:27:14,373 --> 00:27:16,364
是 是 然后呢
Yes, yes, go on.

465
00:27:16,533 --> 00:27:21,812
利润似乎是偷窃来的       什么偷窃?
The profits were the proceeds of theft. Theft?

466
00:27:22,653 --> 00:27:27,602
就是在物主不知道或不许可的情况下取走物品...
I mean removing goods without the knowledgeof the owner...

467
00:27:27,772 --> 00:27:30,765
我知道偷窃的意思 你是什么意思?
I know what theft means. What do YOU mean?

468
00:27:30,932 --> 00:27:33,402
哦 他们送您的凳子
Well, the stool that they gave you

469
00:27:33,573 --> 00:27:37,281
是用偷来的木头做的 来自当地的青年培训车间
was made from wood appropriated from the local YTS workshops.

470
00:27:37,452 --> 00:27:40,844
你是什么意思?      顺出来的
What do you mean? It was nicked.

471
00:27:41,013 --> 00:27:43,243
两名去年的学生干的
By two of last year's pupils.

472
00:27:43,413 --> 00:27:46,370
人赃俱获       谢谢 伯纳
A pair of nickers. Thank you, Bernard.

473
00:27:47,373 --> 00:27:49,682
青年培训车间想要起诉
The YTS want to prosecute.

474
00:27:49,852 --> 00:27:54,131
只有教育部可以阻止他们
Now, the Department of Education could stop them.

475
00:27:54,292 --> 00:27:57,330
您知道 把木料归还 就不声张了
You know, return the wood and hush it up.

476
00:27:57,493 --> 00:27:59,235
汉弗莱 几百万人看到我在电视上
Millions saw me on TV saying

477
00:27:59,235 --> 00:28:01,443
说那学校是全英的楷模
that school was an example!

478
00:28:01,443 --> 00:28:03,772
也算是某种楷模
Well, it is a sort of example.

479
00:28:03,932 --> 00:28:05,685
汉弗莱 他们决不能起诉
They mustn't prosecute!

480
00:28:05,852 --> 00:28:09,255
但愿教育部不会向媒体漏消息
I hope the Department of Education won't leak

481
00:28:09,255 --> 00:28:11,339
说您包庇偷窃行为
the fact that you're covering up for crooks.

482
00:28:11,339 --> 00:28:15,381
你得告诉他们别起诉      那需要他们的配合
You must tell them not to. need their cooperation.

483
00:28:15,381 --> 00:28:21,004
我都能看到报纸头条了 “吉姆的小偷公司”
I can just see the newspapers "Jim's enterprising crooks.

484
00:28:21,173 --> 00:28:26,806
"昔日首相骑墙头 今日落进大墙里"
"The PM has sat on the fence for so long that now he's become one."

485
00:28:28,932 --> 00:28:31,321
劝他们别起诉啊
Persuade them not to prosecute.

486
00:28:31,493 --> 00:28:37,203
已经被判死刑的人可不太听劝
It's very difficult to persuade if they are under a death sentence.

487
00:28:37,373 --> 00:28:40,649
死刑?      您不是要废这个部吗?
Death sentence? If you're abolishing the department.

488
00:28:42,893 --> 00:28:44,690
那个啊
Oh, that!

489
00:28:45,452 --> 00:28:48,763
不 那只是个...模糊的想法...
No, that was just... a vague idea...

490
00:28:50,973 --> 00:28:52,964
...多萝西的
...of Dorothy's.

491
00:28:54,173 --> 00:28:56,368
随便想想 不是认真的
An idle thought. Nothing serious.

492
00:28:56,533 --> 00:28:58,364
您确定吗?      当然了
You're sure? Positive.

493
00:28:58,533 --> 00:29:03,323
太好了 首相 可以谈今天的议程了吗?
Splendid, PM. Shall we now continue with the agendum?

494
00:29:03,493 --> 00:29:06,884
议程? 哦 对
Agendum? Oh, yes!

495
00:29:07,053 --> 00:29:08,884
我们没议程
We have no agendum.

496
00:29:09,053 --> 00:29:12,250
我 们 今 天 没 议 程
(RHYTHMICALLY) We have no agendum today!

497
00:29:14,772 --> 00:29:17,810
本案结束 好吗 汉弗莱?
Business concluded. All right, Humphrey?

498
00:29:18,573 --> 00:29:20,565
是 首相
Yes, PM.

499
00:29:21,258 --> 00:29:31,570
